    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:isDefinedBy"/>
        <IRI>http://webprotege.stanford.edu/RCxNuinhlaH8msIEx2u4KhB</IRI>
        <Literal>The term knowledge management refers to the process of building and managing collective organisational knowledge. It plays a key role in DT and consequently received new attention due to the development of the I4 paradigm. Culture and knowledge management influenced by Collective Intelligence, which refers for the internal knowledge of the organisation. Knowledge Management is the process to support these activities which capabilities are influenced by the Corporate Culture.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:label"/>
        <IRI>http://webprotege.stanford.edu/RCxNuinhlaH8msIEx2u4KhB</IRI>
        <Literal>Culture and knowledge management</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:label"/>
        <IRI>http://webprotege.stanford.edu/RDFJdOuZWPk5flVoo4tOxfS</IRI>
        <Literal>IT management</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:label"/>
        <IRI>http://webprotege.stanford.edu/RDFjrqBiVjwCIBTuWFZ9ECW</IRI>
        <Literal>Structural agility and flexibility</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:label"/>
        <IRI>http://webprotege.stanford.edu/RDLvsAlylbhj9Dk70HE085J</IRI>
        <Literal>IoT and sensors</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:isDefinedBy"/>
        <IRI>http://webprotege.stanford.edu/RDS939Kmovm2MttLkEJ3gbw</IRI>
        <Literal>Collective intelligence incorporates the pooling of skills, knowledge, creativity, thinking, and problem-solving abilities. The synergic combination of these terms facilitated by a collaborative culture and supported by digital tools. 
Key components include competencies, skill acquisition and employee autonomy, competency mapping, competency building, and personnel training to enhance professional abilities and expertise in the C4 era. Health, safety and environmental protection are key elements of CI corporate intelligence</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:label"/>
        <IRI>http://webprotege.stanford.edu/RDS939Kmovm2MttLkEJ3gbw</IRI>
